"Chemours Launches Ti-Pure™ TS-6706, A TMP/TME- Free Version of Flagship Universal Grade, Ti-Pure™ R-706 | Chemours (https://www.chemours.com/en/news-media-center/all-news/press-releases/2025/chemours-launches-ti-pure-ts-6706-a-tmp-tme-free-version-of-flagship-universal-grade-ti-pure-r-706)\nciteturn34search0 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; Wilmington, Del., February 19, 2025 – The Chemours Company (Chemours) (NYSE: CC), a global chemistry company with leading market positions in Thermal & Specialized Solutions (TSS), Titanium Technologies (TT), and Advanced Performance Materials (APM), today announces the launch of Ti-Pure™ TS-6706, a TMP- and TME- free version of Ti-Pure™ R-706 – the benchmark, universal titanium dioxide (TiO₂) grade that works reliably for a variety of coatings applications where appearance is critical.\n\n# Chemours Launches Ti-Pure™ TS-6706, A TMP/TME- Free Version of Flagship Universal Grade, Ti-Pure™ R-706\n\nPress Release\n\nPublished February 19, 2025\n\nWilmington, Del., February 19, 2025 – The Chemours Company (Chemours) (NYSE: CC), a global chemistry company with leading market positions in Thermal & Specialized Solutions (TSS), Titanium Technologies (TT), and Advanced Performance Materials (APM), today announces the launch of Ti-Pure™ TS-6706, a TMP- and TME- free version of Ti-Pure™ R-706 – the benchmark, universal titanium dioxide (TiO₂) grade that works reliably for a variety of coatings applications where appearance is critical.\n\n“As the industry’s trusted TiO₂ partner, we are thrilled to offer a TMP- and TME-free version of our most popular pigment,” said Diane Picho, Interim President, Chemours Titanium Technologies. “The development of Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 is the latest example of our world-class research and development team listening to customers and creating an alternate formulation without sacrificing the quality, consistency, and reliability Chemours is known for.”\n\nDeveloped to address an evolving regulatory climate and deliver solutions that meet customer needs, Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 is part of the Chemours Ti-Pure™ Sustainability Series (TS), dedicated to innovations across four pillars – circularity, climate impact, health and wellness, and resource efficiency.\n\nTi-Pure™ TS-6706 can be used as a drop-in for Ti-Pure™ R-706 with minimal reformulation efforts, as it retains the same physical properties that make the original so universal in the coatings industry – high gloss, excellent durability, blue undertone and hiding power, along with easier dispersion and wet-in. Ti-Pure™ R-706 is prized by formulators for its flexible uses in waterborne, solvent-borne, and powder formulations, and the same flexibility and critical properties are available through Ti-Pure™ TS-6706.\n\nTo ensure optimal performance and ability to meet exacting customer requirements, Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 was tested in both architectural and industrial paint systems, both solvent and water-based. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nChemours führt Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 ein, eine TMP/TME-freie Version der universellen Flagship-Lösung Ti-Pure™ R-706 | Chemours (https://www.chemours.de/news-media-center/all-news/press-releases/2025/chemours-launches-ti-pure-ts-6706-a-tmp-tme-free-version-of-flagship-universal-grade-ti-pure-r-706)\nciteturn34search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Crawled: last month; # Chemours führt Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 ein, eine TMP/TME-freie Version der universellen Flagship-Lösung Ti-Pure™ R-706 ... „Die Entwicklung von Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 ist das jüngste Beispiel dafür, dass unser erstklassiges Forschungs- und Entwicklungsteam auf die Wünsche unserer Kunden eingeht und eine alternative Formulierung entwickelt, ohne dabei die bekannte Qualität, Konsistenz und Zuverlässigkeit von Chemours zu beeinträchtigen.“\n\nAlle Neuigkeiten anzeigen\n\n# Chemours führt Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 ein, eine TMP/TME-freie Version der universellen Flagship-Lösung Ti-Pure™ R-706\n\nPressemeldung\n\nVeröffentlicht Februar 19, 2025\n\nWilmington, Del., 19. Februar 2025 – The Chemours Company (Chemours) (NYSE: CC), ein globales Chemieunternehmen mit führenden Marktpositionen bei Titanium Technologies (TT), Thermal & Specialized Solutions (TSS) und Advanced Performance Materials (APM), gab heute die Markteinführung von Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 bekannt. Dabei handelt es sich um eine TMP- und TME-freie Version von Ti-Pure™ R-706, dem universellen Titandioxid (TiO₂), das sich zuverlässig für eine Vielzahl von Beschichtungsanwendungen eignet, bei denen das Aussehen entscheidend ist.\n\n„Als zuverlässiger TiO₂-Partner der Industrie freuen wir uns sehr, eine TMP- und TME-freie Version unseres beliebtesten Pigments anbieten zu können“, so Diane Picho, Interimspräsidentin von Chemours Titanium Technologies. „Die Entwicklung von Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 ist das jüngste Beispiel dafür, dass unser erstklassiges Forschungs- und Entwicklungsteam auf die Wünsche unserer Kunden eingeht und eine alternative Formulierung entwickelt, ohne dabei die bekannte Qualität, Konsistenz und Zuverlässigkeit von Chemours zu beeinträchtigen.“\n\nTi-Pure™ TS-6706 ist Teil der Chemours Ti-Pure™ Sustainability Series (TS), die auf Innovationen in den vier Bereichen Kreislaufwirtschaft, Klimawirkung, Gesundheit und Wohlbefinden sowie Ressourceneffizienz abzielt. Das Produkt wurde entwickelt, um dem sich verändernden regulatorischen Umfeld Rechnung zu tragen und Lösungen zu liefern, welche die Bedürfnisse der Kunden erfüllen.\n\nTi-Pure™ TS-6706 kann mit minimalem Aufwand als Ersatz für Ti-Pure™ R-706 verwendet werden, da es dieselben physikalischen Eigenschaften wie das universell einsetzbare Original hat: hoher Glanz, ausgezeichnete Haltbarkeit, blauer Unterton und Deckkraft sowie leichtere Dispersion und Benetzung. Ti-Pure™ R-706 wird von Formulierern für seine flexiblen Einsatzmöglichkeiten in wässrigen, lösungsmittelbasierten und pulverförmigen Formulierungen geschätzt. Das neue Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 bietet die gleiche Flexibilität und die gleichen kritischen Eigenschaften.\n\nUm eine optimale Leistungsfähigkeit und die Erfüllung anspruchsvoller Kundenanforderungen zu gewährleisten, wurde Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 in lösemittel- und wasserbasierten Anstrichsystemen für Architektur und Industrie getestet. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nComparisons — SEMITI vs Ti-Pure, Tronox, Kronos & More | TiO2 Agents (https://tio2agents.com/compare)\nciteturn34search2 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; SEMITI 996 vs Ti-Pure R-902 SEMITI 996 is engineered as a 1:1 drop-in substitute for Ti-Pure R-902 in coatings, plastic masterbatch, and inks.Compare →SEMITI 706 vs Ti-Pure R-706 SEMITI 706 matches Ti-Pure R-706's premium durability for industrial and automotive coatings — at 35–40% lower landed cost.Compare →SEMITI 902 vs Ti-Pure R-902 SEMITI 902 is specifically engineered to drop into Ti-Pure R-902-qualified architectural paint formulations.Compare →SEMITI 706W vs Ti-Pure R-746 SEMITI 706W matches Ti-Pure R-746 as a hydrophilic-tuned rutile for waterborne architectural emulsion paints.Compare →SEMITI 960 vs Ti-Pure R-960 SEMITI 960 matches Ti-Pure R-960's amine-compatible HALS-friendly surface treatment for engineering plastics masterbatch.Compare →SEMITI INK-1 vs Ti-Pure R-931 SEMITI INK-1 matches Ti-Pure R-931 as an easy-dispersion ink-grade rutile for offset, flexo, gravure, and UV inks.Compare →SEMITI PAPER-D vs Ti-Pure R-104 SEMITI PAPER-D matches Ti-Pure R-104 as a decor and laminate paper-grade rutile.Compare →SEMITI 2310 vs Ti-Pure R-902 SEMITI 2310 is plastics-specific; Ti-Pure R-902 is universal coatings/plastics.\n\nCompare\n\n# SEMITI vs the global TiO2 reference brands\n\nWhen formulators evaluate substituting one TiO2 grade for another, they look at three things: matched performance specs, drop-in compatibility with existing formulations, and the cost gap. Each comparison page below answers all three for a specific SEMITI grade vs the corresponding international reference grade — with side-by-side spec tables, when-to-choose decision criteria, and pricing context.\n\n## SEMITI vs Chemours\n\nSEMITI 996 vs Ti-Pure R-902 SEMITI 996 is engineered as a 1:1 drop-in substitute for Ti-Pure R-902 in coatings, plastic masterbatch, and inks.Compare →SEMITI 706 vs Ti-Pure R-706 SEMITI 706 matches Ti-Pure R-706's premium durability for industrial and automotive coatings — at 35–40% lower landed cost.Compare →SEMITI 902 vs Ti-Pure R-902 SEMITI 902 is specifically engineered to drop into Ti-Pure R-902-qualified architectural paint formulations.Compare →SEMITI 706W vs Ti-Pure R-746 SEMITI 706W matches Ti-Pure R-746 as a hydrophilic-tuned rutile for waterborne architectural emulsion paints.Compare →SEMITI 960 vs Ti-Pure R-960 SEMITI 960 matches Ti-Pure R-960's amine-compatible HALS-friendly surface treatment for engineering plastics masterbatch.Compare →SEMITI INK-1 vs Ti-Pure R-931 SEMITI INK-1 matches Ti-Pure R-931 as an easy-dispersion ink-grade rutile for offset, flexo, gravure, and UV inks.Compare →SEMITI PAPER-D vs Ti-Pure R-104 SEMITI PAPER-D matches Ti-Pure R-104 as a decor and laminate paper-grade rutile.Compare →【7†SEMITI 2310 vs Ti-Pure R-902 SEMITI 2310 is plastics-specific; Ti-Pure R-902 is universal coatings/plastics. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTitanium Dioxide Manufacturer | Ti-Pure™ TiO₂ by Chemours | Products (https://www.tipure.com/en/products)\nciteturn34search3 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 This universal grade is a TMP/ TME- free version of Ti-Pure™ R-706.\nLearn more about Ti-Pure™ for Coatings.\n\nTo find the right grade for your needs, download the Grade Selection Guide.\n\nTi-Pure™ R-706 This universal grade performs dependably for many demanding applications. Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 This universal grade is a TMP/ TME- free version of Ti-Pure™ R-706. Performs dependably for many demanding applications. Ti-Pure™ R-900 This versatile TiO₂ pigment adds whiteness and brightness to interior paints. Ti-Pure™ R-960 This TiO₂ improves color retention and strengthens weatherability for paints. Ti-Pure™ TS-6200 Designed to advance sustainability in the most demanding coating applications by maximizing resource efficiency through extended product life and avoided waste. Ti-Pure™ TS-6300 A high-opacity pigment for coatings applications that enables superior hiding power and reduced resource consumption and waste in the painting process. 【8†Ti-Pure™ R-746 This slurry has good color matching and durability. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTitanium Dioxide Solutions for Coatings | Ti-Pure™ TiO₂ by Chemours (https://www.tipure.com/en/products/coatings)\nciteturn34search4 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 6 days ago; Two multipurpose gloss grades, Ti-Pure™ R-706 and Ti-Pure™ R-902+, are recommended for use when a single pigment is required to perform well in both interior and exterior gloss and semi-gloss systems. ... Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 This universal grade is a TMP/ TME- free version of Ti-Pure™ R-706.\n\n\n## Titanium Dioxide Uses\n\n### Titanium Dioxide for Paints\n\n#### Gloss and Semigloss Paints\n\nTi-Pure™ R-900 is recommended for general use in alkyd and latex paints for interior gloss and semi-gloss applications. This pigment disperses easily, develops high gloss and shows maximum hiding power over a wide range of gloss grade applications.\n\nTwo multipurpose gloss grades, Ti-Pure™ R-706 and Ti-Pure™ R-902+, are recommended for use when a single pigment is required to perform well in both interior and exterior gloss and semi-gloss systems. R-706 is the ideal selection for applications requiring high gloss, maximum gloss retention and chalk resistance. Both R-706 and R-902+ will deliver bright, clean colors in tinted systems with R-706 providing a blue undertone and R-902+ providing a more neutral undertone.\n\nFor paint manufacturers capable of handling TiO₂ in aqueous slurry form, Ti-Pure™ R-706 and R-902+ are available as slurry grades, Ti-Pure™ R-746 and R-942 respectively.\n\n#### Flat Paints\n\nThese coatings are formulated at relatively high levels of extenders and TiO₂ pigments, and are frequently above the critical PVC for interior applications. To support your individual formulation needs, our technical service laboratories are fully equipped to assist you (Figure 20).\n\n### Samples/Order Placement\n\nSamples of dry and slurry Ti-Pure™ titanium dioxide grades are readily available from www.titnaium.chemours.com and are recommended for your use in product development and testing. To place an order, please contact your local representative.\n\n### Ti-Pure™ Titanium Dioxide Products for Coatings\n\nTi-Pure™ R-706 This universal grade performs dependably for many demanding applications. Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 This universal grade is a TMP/ TME- free version of Ti-Pure™ R-706. Performs dependably for many demanding applications. Ti-Pure™ R-900 This versatile TiO₂ pigment adds whiteness and brightness to interior paints. Ti-Pure™ R-960 This TiO₂ improves color retention and strengthens weatherability for paints. Ti-Pure™ TS-6200 Designed to advance sustainability in the most demanding coating applications by maximizing resource efficiency through extended product life and avoided waste. --------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTires Pyrolysis - The Chemours Company (Chemours), a global leader in Thermal & Specialized Solutions, Titanium Technologies, and Advanced Performance Materials, has introduced Ti-Pure™ TS-6706, a TMP- and TME-free alternative to its widely used Ti-Pure™ R-706. This launch offers a regulatory-compliant solution while maintaining the high-performance characteristics essential for coatings applications 24-02-2025 • Polyestertime (https://www.polyestertime.com/tires-pyrolysis/)\nciteturn34search5 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Crawled: 2 days ago; #### The Chemours Company (Chemours), a global leader in Thermal & Specialized Solutions, Titanium Technologies, and Advanced Performance Materials, has introduced Ti-Pure™ TS-6706, a TMP- and TME-free alternative to its widely used Ti-Pure™ R-706.\n# Chemours Unveils Ti-Pure™ TS-6706: A TMP/TME-Free Alternative to Ti-Pure™ R-706\n\n#### The Chemours Company (Chemours), a global leader in Thermal & Specialized Solutions, Titanium Technologies, and Advanced Performance Materials, has introduced Ti-Pure™ TS-6706, a TMP- and TME-free alternative to its widely used Ti-Pure™ R-706. This launch offers a regulatory-compliant solution while maintaining the high-performance characteristics essential for coatings applications.\n\nDelivering Quality Without Compromise\n\n“As a trusted TiO2 partner, we are excited to provide a TMP- and TME-free version of our flagship pigment,” said Diane Picho, Interim President of Chemours Titanium Technologies. “Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 is a testament to our commitment to customer needs, offering an alternative formulation without sacrificing quality, consistency, or performance.”\n\nTi-Pure™ TS-6706 is part of the Chemours Ti-Pure™ Sustainability Series (TS), which drives innovation across four pillars: circularity, climate impact, health and wellness, and resource efficiency. This development aligns with the industry’s evolving regulatory landscape while ensuring continued product excellence.  Tires Pyrolysis\n\nSeamless Transition for Formulators\n\nDesigned as a direct replacement for Ti-Pure™ R-706, Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 requires minimal reformulation, as it retains the same core properties. These include high gloss, excellent durability, blue undertone, superior hiding power, and easy dispersion. It offers the same versatility as its predecessor, supporting waterborne, solvent-borne, and powder coatings.\n\nTo ensure optimal performance, Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 has been rigorously tested in both architectural and industrial paint systems, covering solvent- and water-based formulations. Evaluations focused on key performance attributes such as viscosity stability, color consistency, gloss, tinting strength, hiding power, and mechanical durability post-application. Tires Pyrolysis\n\nEnsuring Reliable Performance\n\nGiven TMP’s role in dry pigment flow, extensive testing was conducted at both lab and industrial scales to assess flow behavior, including in-silo conditions. The results confirmed that Ti-Pure™ TS-6706 meets the high standards expected by formulators.\n\nBy delivering a TMP- and TME-free alternative without compromising on performance, Chemours continues to lead the way in innovative TiO2 solutions, supporting both industry needs and sustainability goals. Tires Pyrolysis\n\nImage: Chemours Unveils Ti-Pure™ TS-6706: A TMP/TME-Free Alternative to Ti-Pure™ R-7067\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTiO2Basics for Paint Appearance and Performance | PCI Magazine (https://www.pcimag.com/articles/83622-tio2basics-for-paint-appearance-and-performance)\nciteturn34search6 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: yesterday; Ti-Pure R-706 and R-902 are recommended for use when a single pigment is required to perform well in both interior and exterior gloss and semigloss systems. ... Ti-Pure R-706 is the most widely applicable grade, possessing a combination of exceptionally high gloss and excellent exterior durability unique in the industry.\nAlthough high hiding is important in all coatings, grade choice often depends on the gloss level and exterior durability required.\n\nTi-Pure R-706 is the most widely applicable grade, possessing a combination of exceptionally high gloss and excellent exterior durability unique in the industry. It can be used in both interior and exterior coatings where this combination of gloss and durability combined with excellent dispersibility is of value. R-960, although lower in gloss than R-706, provides outstanding chalk resistance and tint retention and should be used in premium-quality exterior finishes where resistance to chalking and color change are of primary importance. Applications include coil coatings for residential aluminum siding and architectural building panels, aerospace coatings, and other high-durability applications. Because of their silica surface treatment, both of these grades provide better film cure in acid-catalyzed coatings than nonsilica-treated grades.\n\nTi-Pure R-902 is used in high-quality finishes that require very good chalk resistance and gloss retention, but not the exceptional performance provided by R-706 and R-960. This grade is often used in industrial maintenance, implement and transportation finishes, and some container coatings.\n\nTi-Pure R-700 and R-900 are both used primarily for interior coating applications. R-700 is recommended for most applications and provides the highest gloss combined with a blue undertone for clean tints. Compared with R-900, R-700 provides better film cure in acid-catalyzed coatings because of its neutral pH and lower level of alumina surface treatment. R-900 is widely used for can coatings where its neutral undertone and high gloss are valued. Applications for both grades include appliance coatings, metal furniture finishes, and high-reflectance white coil coatings.\n\nImageCourtesy of DuPont Titanium Technologies\n\nFigure 2: TiO2 Particle Size and Distribution Effect on Properties\n\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTitanium Dioxide for Architectural & Automative Coatings | R-706 | TiO₂ (https://www.tipure.com/en/products/coatings/r-706)\nciteturn34search7 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: last week; Ti-Pure™ R-706 is a rutile titanium dioxide (TiO₂) pigment that is a benchmark grade for interior and exterior coatings.\n\n# Ti-Pure™ R-706\n\nImage: person climbing a ladder against a home exterior with paint can\n\n## Consistency and Flexibility When Appearances Matter \n\nTi-Pure™ R-706 is a rutile titanium dioxide (TiO₂) pigment that is a benchmark grade for interior and exterior coatings. It provides flexibility and reliability for applications and formulations where appearance is critical.\n\n### Features and Benefits\n\nManufactured via a proprietary chloride process, Ti-Pure™ R-706 features:\n\n  * Tight particular size control for color match confidence\n  * Blue undertone for maximum flexibility in formulated color space and brighter, cleaner colors in tinted systems\n  * Balance of properties for reliability and flexibility in high-performance applications\n  * Enhanced durability for superior gloss retention so coatings look new longer\n  * Silica treatment for better film cure in acid catalyzed coatings\n\n### Applications for Ti-Pure™ R-706\n\nTi-Pure™ R-706 is frequently found in:\n\n  * Gloss and semi-gloss architectural paints\n--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\n科慕发布 Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）TS-6706——旗舰通用产品 Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）R-706 的不含 TMP 和 TME 的版本 | Chemours (https://www.chemours.cn/news-media-center/all-news/press-releases/2025/chemours-launches-ti-pure-ts-6706-a-tmp-tme-free-version-of-flagship-universal-grade-ti-pure-r-706)\nciteturn34search8 [wordlim: 200] Published: 1.5 years ago; Crawled: yesterday; # 科慕发布 Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）TS-6706——旗舰通用产品 Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）R-706 的不含 TMP 和 TME 的版本\n\nTi-Pure™（淳泰™）TS-6706 属于科慕 Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）可持续系列 (TS) 的一部分，旨在应对不断变化的监管环境和提供满足客户需求的解决方案。可持续系列致力于在循环性、气候影响、卫生和健康以及资源效率这四大支柱领域进行创新。\n\nTi-Pure™（淳泰™）TS-6706 可以作为 Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）R-706 的替代产品，但无需费力重新配方，因为它保留了使原版产品通用于涂料行业的物理属性，即高光泽度、优异耐久性、蓝色底色和遮盖力，而且它更容易分散和浸润。Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）R-706 因其在水性、溶剂型和粉末配方中的灵活运用而备受配方设计师珍视，而 Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）TS-6706 同样具有这种灵活性和重要属性。\n\n为了确保最佳性能并满足严格的客户要求，Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）TS-6706 在建筑和工业涂料系统中均进行了测试，包括溶剂和水性测试。Ti-Pure™（淳泰™）TS-6706 还就其对关键参数的影响进行了评估，如液体涂料的粘度稳定性，以及涂料应用后的颜色、光泽度、着色强度、遮盖力和机械强度。--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nTitanium Dioxide 